# Chain Graph

Purpose:
  Unbreakable chain graph for SDDRA. Every execution path is a branch of `default`.
  Arms return to parent; rules and tokens flow through every node.

Node ID short rules:
  2-6 chars. Example: `D0`, `P1`, `S1`, `C1`, `R1`, `DEP1`.

Nodes:
  D0  default
  P1  prompt
  D1  docs
  S1  sdd
  C1  code
  R1  review
  DEP1 deploy

Edges:
  D0->P1
  D0->D1
  D0->S1
  D0->C1
  D0->R1
  D0->DEP1
  P1->D0
  D1->D0
  S1->D0
  C1->D0
  R1->D0
  DEP1->D0

Property:
  graph.type = cyclic
  graph.root = D0
  graph.arms = P1,D1,S1,C1,R1,DEP1
  graph.rules = ./rules/INDEX.sdd
  graph.tokens = ../../projects/example_project/tokens/INDEX.sdd

State: +

